 {
  "id": "mltab",
  "type": "tab",
  "label": "ML Control",
  "disabled": false,
  "info": "Buttons for the Python ML service (ml/ml-service.py, listening on 127.0.0.1:9100).\n\nWorkflow (regression, like fluid.mlpregressor):\n  1. Put the inputs in a state (freeze tv.m = 0.1) and set the target (manual: cassette m = ...).\n  2. Click 'record' -> one training pair (current inputs -> current targets).\n  3. Repeat for several states. 4. 'train'. 5. 'predict on'.\n  Predictions arrive at the hub as /ml/cassette/m and the routing table forwards them to the cassette.\n\nStatus lines from the service appear in the hub registry under device 'ml' (param 'status')."
 },
